Subject: The unit can ask which method a shape finds

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_shape_method(shape, atom, &value)` (exported to the units, declared in quickjs-aot-rt.h) returns 1 and the function object a receiver of `shape` finds as `atom` on its prototype chain, when the shape has no own property of that name and the first prototype object that has it holds it as a plain data property; else 0.

Why we need it
  A compiled copy inside a switch arm knows its receiver's shape, so the methods it calls on `this` are known too: the arm resolves them once per cache epoch, with the entry each is bound to, and the copy's calls on them compare that entry instead of walking the callee's cache cells and testing the callee's identity on every iteration.

Soundness
  It reads the shape and ordinary prototype objects only (no getter runs, no allocation). The unit keeps the answer while `shape_free_epoch` (0420) and `aot_pic_epoch` have not moved; every write that can change what a prototype holds, or a prototype link, moves the latter, which is the same contract the constructor-wrapper cache (`qjs_aot_wrap_init`) relies on.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_shape_method` (new).

No.

--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -231,0 +232,2 @@
+/* the function a receiver of `shape` finds as `atom` on its prototype chain, when it is a plain data property (a compiled copy resolves its receiver's methods from the shape) */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_shape_method(const void *shape, uint32_t atom, JSValue *out);
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65286,0 +65287,39 @@
+/* The method a receiver of shape `shape` finds as `atom`: 1 with the value when the shape has no own property of that name and the first
+   object of its prototype chain that has one holds it as a plain data property (ordinary objects only, at most eight links), else 0.
+   Like qjs_aot_shape_slot it reads the shape and the prototype objects only, so the caller keeps the answer while shape_free_epoch
+   and aot_pic_epoch have not moved (every write that can change what a prototype holds, or a prototype link, moves the latter). */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_shape_method(const void *shape, uint32_t atom, JSValue *out)
+{
+    JSShape *sh = (JSShape *)shape;
+    JSShapeProperty *prop, *prs;
+    JSProperty *pr;
+    JSObject *holder;
+    intptr_t h;
+    int depth;
+
+    if (sh == NULL)
+        return 0;
+    h = (uintptr_t)atom & sh->prop_hash_mask;
+    h = prop_hash_end(sh)[-h - 1];
+    prop = get_shape_prop(sh);
+    while (h) {
+        if (prop[h - 1].atom == (JSAtom)atom)
+            return 0;
+        h = prop[h - 1].hash_next;
+    }
+    holder = sh->proto;
+    for (depth = 0; holder != NULL; depth++) {
+        if (depth >= 8 || holder->class_id != JS_CLASS_OBJECT || holder->is_exotic)
+            return 0;
+        prs = find_own_property(&pr, holder, (JSAtom)atom);
+        if (prs != NULL) {
+            if ((prs->flags & JS_PROP_TMASK) != JS_PROP_NORMAL || JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(pr->u.value) != JS_TAG_OBJECT)
+                return 0;
+            *out = pr->u.value;
+            return 1;
+        }
+        holder = holder->shape->proto;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
